@startuml logic-overlay-server
title UniChat — OBS overlay HTTP/WebSocket server (reference logic from master)

actor Streamer
boundary "OBS Browser Source" as OBS
participant "overlay.command" as CMD
participant "OverlayServerService\n(overlay-server-service.service.rs)" as SRV
participant "overlay-router.service.rs" as RT
participant "overlay-subscriber-manager.service.rs" as SUB
participant "overlay-ws-handlers.service.rs" as WSH
database "storage (overlay config)" as ST

Streamer -> CMD: start_overlay_server()
SRV -> SRV: bind 127.0.0.1:<OVERLAY_SERVER_PORT>\nserve built frontend dist (static assets)
CMD -> ST: init_overlay_config_from_storage()\n-> OverlayConfig{ sources[], theme, layout }
Streamer -> CMD: open_overlay_window()\n(Tauri WebviewWindow preview)

OBS -> RT: GET /overlay (browser source URL)
RT -> SUB: register viewer; upgrade to WebSocket
WSH --> OBS: snapshot OverlayConfig + recent OverlayMessages

loop live chat flow
  [IRC/Kick/YT ingestion] -> ST: append normalized OverlayMessage
  CMD -> SUB: emit_overlay_config_changed(config)\non config edit
  SUB -> WSH: broadcast to all subscribers
  WSH --> OBS: WS push: new message / config delta
  OBS -> OBS: render animated chat overlay
end

Streamer -> CMD: stop_overlay_server()
SRV -> SUB: drop subscribers, unbind port

Failure rules (master):
- port already bound -> command returns error, UI shows banner
- malformed source entry in config -> skipped with warning, others kept

note over CMD: dioxus-migration status: handlers start/stop/open/config exist as stubs\nreturning success; no listener is ever started.\nSDUI page renders controls but they mutate nothing.
@enduml
